   "notes": "6-11 Sidney St (M&S): Edwardian red-brick upper floors with white stone window architraves and pilaster strips over a modern full-width shopfront (grey stone/glass, recessed entrance) with 'Marks & Spencer' in dark green letters on a grey fascia band. Bay count (11, ~3.1 m pitch) estimated from oblique views; the street photos suggest a further attic storey above the 11.3 m eave (OSM footprint sits ~4 m behind the street line) which is not modelled."
