   "notes": "Marks & Spencer rear/service elevation on Hobson St (tagged Sidney St by address). Plain red brick with white painted/stone bands at first- and second-floor level and a projecting eaves gutter; ground floor has recessed blind brick panels with stone sills (modelled as dark low windows) and a service entrance with a Marks & Spencer sign near the south end; tall white-framed multi-pane metal windows on the upper floors. Seen only obliquely, so bay spacing is estimated."
